  "body": "This might be a bad suggestion, but having an attribute `link` to an image, could lead to better redirects. Having an attribute like that could potentially help pages being seen better, as it is more approachable. However, having this attribute would need specific criteria's, as it also could lead to redirects to pages that aren't potentially the right one. \n\nFor an instance, Twitter could benefit from this, reducing characters in an tweet when you swap out the url in a tweet, you could rather apply to something relative, if the post is blank, like in this use case, an image with an url( and say, an indication that it's clickable, like an blue frame around it)\n\nThere is a lot to consider from this, so I want to hear your input on this, \n\nES\n",
